comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T21:59:23.505Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check 2026-07-13: prior all-status audits are completed point-in-time reviews and pm-e9zh owns terminal resolution evidence; none owns a future resumable typed-relationship reconstruction program. This plan starts only after pm-6x7o."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T00:00:23.513Z",maintainer-agent,"Depth baseline measured 2026-07-25, before and after an active-graph enrichment pass. This is the first census that separates semantic edges from hierarchy, which turns out to be the measurement that matters.\n\nMethod. Parse every item file directly for parent and dependency edges, build two undirected graphs — one over all edge kinds, one excluding parent and child — and run breadth-first search from the outcome milestone roots over each. Hierarchy-inclusive reachability flatters the graph badly, so it is reported separately and should not be used as a health signal.\n\nBefore, over 218 active items: 2 items with zero semantic edges, both of them capability epics (the MCP platform epic and the observability epic — the two hubs least likely to be suspected); 57 items with exactly one; 44 items unreachable from any outcome milestone by semantic edges alone; maximum semantic hop distance 3, with hierarchy carrying almost all of the apparent connectivity.\n\nAfter: zero items with no semantic edge; 29 with exactly one, of which 27 are Semgrep findings sitting correctly in their deliberate two-level rule-class hub topology and one is the recorded deliberately-shallow item that must never receive fabricated edges; 0 unreachable; semantic hop distance now distributes across 0 to 6, meaning traversal actually traverses. Workspace edge count moved 3,478 to 3,764, entirely in the related kind and entirely on active items.\n\nThe finding worth keeping. The audit's isolated-node and degree-at-most-one counters both read zero before this pass, while 44 active items could not reach any strategic outcome without walking a parent edge. Those counters measure whether an item is attached, not whether it is explained. Depth, eccentricity, and shortest typed path to an outcome are the properties that make graph algorithms useful for context assembly, and none of them were being measured. That gap is now owned by pm-bzmeaa.\n\nConstraint honoured. No closed or canceled item was touched in this pass. Terminal lineage remains the exclusive territory of the dedicated changelog-safe waves — pm-lnrk for closed lineage, pm-hnc9w7 for legacy edge hygiene, pm-s5e04g for evidence-derived edges — precisely because touching a terminal item moves its timestamp and drags years-old work into the current release notes."
body: "## Wave strategy\n\n0. Freeze and publish a reproducible baseline; classify current roots, active dependency isolates, aliases, and body-to-edge mismatches.\n1. Enrich active strategic stories, features, decisions, and delivery chains with high-confidence explicit evidence.\n2. Normalize legacy edge aliases and repair semantic integrity after ADR acceptance.\n3. Backfill recent terminal lineages in changelog-safe batches, then move backward by history epoch.\n4. Reconstruct evidence, incident, release, package, and domain relationships from immutable events and linked resources.\n5. Verify million-item and federated behavior, sample quality manually, and retain a waiver and uncertainty ledger.\n\n## Safety\n\nNo generic-density target. No all-items full dump. No terminal touch outside a dedicated batch. No automatic edge whose source and confidence cannot be explained. A correction appends a superseding event rather than erasing proof."
